  "CREATE DEFINER='mysql.sys'@'localhost' FUNCTION extract_schema_from_file_name ( path VARCHAR(512) ) RETURNS VARCHAR(64) COMMENT ' Description ----------- Takes a raw file path, and attempts to extract the schema name from it. Useful for when interacting with Performance Schema data concerning IO statistics, for example. Currently relies on the fact that a table data file will be within a specified database directory (will not work with partitions or tables that specify an individual DATA_DIRECTORY). Parameters ----------- path (VARCHAR(512)): The full file path to a data file to extract the schema name from. Returns ----------- VARCHAR(64) Example ----------- mysql> SELECT sys.extract_schema_from_file_name(\\'/var/lib/mysql/employees/employee.ibd\\'); +----------------------------------------------------------------------------+ | sys.extract_schema_from_file_name(\\'/var/lib/mysql/employees/employee.ibd\\') | +----------------------------------------------------------------------------+ | employees | +----------------------------------------------------------------------------+ 1 row in set (0.00 sec) ' SQL SECURITY INVOKER DETERMINISTIC NO SQL BEGIN RETURN LEFT(SUBSTRING_INDEX(SUBSTRING_INDEX(REPLACE(path, '\\\\', '/'), '/', -2), '/', 1), 64); END"
